LICENSE — PENDING OWNER DECISION
==================================

No license has been chosen for this project yet.

This file is a placeholder created as part of RE-1 (Release Engineering,
Repository Hygiene & Governance Foundation) so that repository tooling
(GitHub's own license detection, dependency/compliance scanners, etc.) has
a LICENSE file to find, and so the absence of a license is visible and
explicit rather than silent.

Choosing a license is a business/legal decision, not an engineering one,
and has deliberately NOT been made here. Relevant existing signal: the
Windows desktop app's `tools/device-manager/package.json` currently
declares `"license": "UNLICENSED"` and `"private": true`, which is
consistent with — but not a substitute for — an explicit decision at the
project level.

Until an owner decision is recorded here, treat this codebase as
**all rights reserved**: no permission is granted to copy, modify,
distribute, or use this software outside of what the repository owner
has separately, explicitly authorized.

ACTION REQUIRED: the repository owner should replace this file with the
actual chosen license text (e.g. MIT, Apache-2.0, a proprietary/commercial
license, etc.) or explicitly confirm "all rights reserved, no open license"
as the final decision.
